# netsurf: a typeless :*-of-type rule reaches only children of a tag that went in (patch 507)
# Generated 2026-11-28
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 506)
#
# html_rl_block_struct_risk counted a typeless :nth-of-type /
# :first-of-type / :last-of-type compound (of_type, no tag) as able to flip
# every child in the change's range. Such a rule counts each child among
# its own tag only, so it can flip only a child whose tag went in or out.
# The moved tags are known only when nothing was removed (a removed element
# with no box leaves no tag), so the check applies to insertions only.
# Seen on stackoverflow: scripts append to <html>, and a "*:nth-of-type"
# rule counted <body> as moved -- the narrow answer then restyled all of
# <body>.
#
# Gate: JS-nth-type / CSS-nth-type-ref (four steps, row for row against the
# same steps at parse time). Every existing structural gate page gives the
# same counts on 506 and 507 (checked before gating).
